Rumors about Apple's work on a touchscreen <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> started in 2023, when <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> said there <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/01/11/touchscreen-macs-report/">would be a MacBook Pro</a> with an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; display and a touchscreen, but &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; rumors date back even further. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/oled-macbook-pro-display.jpg" alt="" width="2390" height="1344" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1074257" /><br/>
We heard a lot about the new Mac over the last few years, and we thought we'd take a look back to see what was right and what was wrong.<br/>
<h2>OLED</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2016</strong> - In 2016, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2016/11/01/future-macbooks-oled-displays/"><em>ETNews</em> said</a> Apple was considering &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; displays for future MacBooks.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2019</strong> - <em>The Elec</em> said Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2019/05/23/samsung-oled-16-inch-macbook-pro-rumor/">was in talks</a> with Samsung about &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; displays for a future 16-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2021</strong> - <em>The Elec</em> said a future MacBook would use an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; display with a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2021/11/03/future-ipad-pro-macbook-pro-oled-displays/">two-stack tandem structure</a>, which is what Apple announced today.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2023</strong> - <em>ETNews</em> claimed Apple was <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/01/20/apple-work-oled-for-ipad-macbook/">sourcing OLED panels</a> in 14-inch and 16-inch sizes for the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;, which turned out to be accurate.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2023</strong> - Apple analyst <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ming-chi-kuo/">Ming-Chi Kuo</a> said Apple would release the first MacBook with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/01/10/oled-macbook-kuo/">an OLED display</a> by the end of 2024 at the earliest, which was incorrect.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Touch</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2023</strong> - <em>Bloomberg</em>'s &zwnj;Mark Gurman&zwnj; was the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/01/11/touchscreen-macs-report/">first to report</a> on a touch display. In January 2023, he said Apple was working on an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; with a touchscreen.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - Kuo <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/17/kuo-2026-oled-macbook-pro-touch-panel/">said in September 2025</a> that the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would have touch sensors integrated into the display panel's top layer, which was correct.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>No Notch/Dynamic Island</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2024</strong> - Omdia <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/12/09/macbook-pro-without-notch-roadmap/">said in December 2024</a> that Apple would remove the notch from the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; "in a few years," replacing it with a hole-punch camera. The hole-punch aspect wasn't quite correct.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - In August 2025, Omdia said an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; MacBook coming in 2026 would have an iPhone-like <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a> cutout <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/08/07/oled-macbook-pro-display-cutout-no-notch/">instead of a notch</a>.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - In October 2025, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/16/macbook-pro-oled-touch-screen/">Gurman said</a> the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would have a "so-called hole-punch design" with a "display area around the sensor" similar to the &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj;.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - In February 2026, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/24/touchscreen-macbook-pro-dynamic-island/">Gurman described</a> the &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj; as interactive and able to contextually expand based on the app or Mac feature in use.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Hinge</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - Gurman was the first to mention a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/16/macbook-pro-oled-touch-screen/">reinforced hinge</a> that would keep the display from moving when touched.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Design</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2024</strong> - In November 2024, Gurman said the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would have a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/11/03/future-macbook-pro-rumors/">thinner design</a>, which was accurate.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - In October 2026, Gurman said he didn't expect the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/08/oled-macbook-pro-wont-be-thinner/">would be</a> "significantly thinner," tempering expectations.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - In October 2026, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/04/oled-macbook-pro-significantly-lighter-rumor/">he said</a> the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models would be "significantly lighter."</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Chips</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - In October 2025, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/16/macbook-pro-oled-touch-screen/">Gurman predicted</a> the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models would use M6-series chips, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/10/oled-display-m6-pro-max-macbook-pro/">in November</a>, he specified M6 Pro and M6 Max chips.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - In June 2026, Gurman said there would be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/26/oled-macbook-stick-with-m5-pro-and-m5-max/">no M6 Pro or M6 Max chips</a>, and the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would instead use M5 Pro and M5 Max chips.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - In September 2026, Omdia said the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would have an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/03/macbook-ultra-m5-ultra-chip-rumor/">M5 Ultra chip option</a>, which was wrong.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Pricing</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - In March 2026, Gurman said the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/08/apple-planning-macbook-ultra/">would be more expensive</a> and would be above the mini-LED &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models, which was correct.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2026</strong> - Just a day before the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models were announced, Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/27/oled-macbook-pro-pricing/">accurately predicted</a> the &#36;2,899 and &#36;3,399 pricing.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Naming</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>March 2026</strong> - Gurman suggested Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/08/apple-planning-macbook-ultra/">was working on</a> a "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">MacBook Ultra</a>," but he did hedge and say Apple might not use the Ultra naming.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>April 2026</strong> - <em>Macworld</em> claimed Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/27/apple-planning-to-launch-two-new-ultra-products/">would release</a> a &zwnj;MacBook Ultra&zwnj; in late 2026 or early 2027.</li><br/>
<li><strong>October 2026</strong> - <em>MacRumors</em>' Joe Rossignol speculated that Apple could <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/28/macbook-studio/">call the new MacBook</a> the "MacBook Studio," but that didn't happen.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Launch Timing</h2><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>2021</strong> - In March 2021, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2021/03/04/ipad-macbook-oled-displays-2022-rumor/"><em>DigiTimes</em> said</a> Apple would release &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models with an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; display in 2022, which was not accurate.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2021</strong> - In November 2021, <em>The Elec</em> said an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would launch in 2025, but <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2021/11/03/future-ipad-pro-macbook-pro-oled-displays/">also suggested</a> the launch could be postponed.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2023</strong> - When Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/01/11/touchscreen-macs-report/">first reported</a> on the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;, he said it would launch in 2025.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2023</strong> - In March 2023, display analyst Ross Young accurately predicted Apple would <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/03/30/13-4-inch-oled-macbook-air-rumor/">launch an OLED MacBook Pro</a> in 2026, but he also incorrectly claimed an &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-air/">MacBook Air</a> would come first in 2024.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2024</strong> - In November 2024, Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/11/03/future-macbook-pro-rumors/">updated launch timing</a> to "probably" 2026.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - In August 2025, <em>Dealsite.co.kr</em> said <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/08/07/macbook-pro-oled-display-launch-late-next-year/">Apple would launch</a> a &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; with &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; in late 2026, which was accurate.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - In September 2025, <em>The Elec</em> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/09/oled-macbook-pro-coming-next-year/">also said</a> the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would launch in the fourth quarter of 2026.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2025</strong> - In October 2025, Gurman updated his launch timing prediction to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/16/macbook-pro-oled-touch-screen/">late 2026 or early 2027</a>.</li><br/>
<li><strong>2026</strong> - In February 2026, Gurman said the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; would <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/24/touchscreen-macbook-pro-dynamic-island/">launch in 2026</a>, though in April he went back to 2026 to 2027 and said the touchscreen &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; launch timing could <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/19/when-to-expect-next-macbook-pro-and-mac-studio/">slip to the end</a> of his predicted window because of the chip shortage. By September, he <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/oled-macbook-pro-macos-27-1-testing/">updated timing</a> to "later this year," and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/15/touchscreen-macbook-pro-november-6/">he mentioned</a> a November 6 launch on October 15.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Not Rumored</h2><br/>
Some features in the new &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; were never rumored and came as a surprise.<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li>Illuminated Apple logo</li><br/>
 	<li>Up to 16TB storage</li><br/>
 	<li>Revamped speakers</li><br/>
 	<li>PROLED XDR naming</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2>Wrap Up</h2><br/>
